1.The image is converted into a pixel matrix to feed an image to our model which is further converted into an array of numbers.

2.The simple ANN classifier works perfectly in cases where digit is at the center of the image.Still, it fails to identify if the digit is slightly distorted or when
placed at a different position in the image.

3.It is part of the image or feature on which we are looking at deciding the impression created in the brain.

4.A CNN model interprets a grayscale image as a 2-D array.Each array element corresponds to a pixel value ranging between 0(white color) and 255(black).

5.The color images are represented as a 3-D array consisting of red, green, blue(RGB channels).By combining these channels, we get the pixel value of our colored
image.Pixel values in each channel also lie between 0 and 255.

6. 2 primary components of CNN model:
  i. Convolutional part
  ii. Final Classificatio part

7.In general,CNN model works in following steps:
  i. Convolution layer : It takes two inputs i) image matrix and ii) feature detector or filter or kernel. Convolution is a mathematical operation.The shifting of the
     image patch extractor by one pixel is the stride.The feature maps are known as convolved features.Multiple feature detector convolves over the input image producing
     a layer of feature maps which form a single convolutional layer.The neural network (not engineers) implicitly decides values of these filters used in a convolutional 
     layer.The main objective of convolution is to find important features in the image.
     -> Rectified Linear Unit(ReLU) introduces non-linearity to the network,allowing it to learn complex patterns and relationships in the data.
  ii. Pooling : Firstly,it is used to capture the vital feature irrespective of their location or position.Secondly,it is used to reduce the size of the feature map,
      which makes the processing faster by including important information only.Pooling also avoids overfitting.
  iii. Flattening : The pooled feature maps are flattened into a 1D vector that inputs the subsequent ANN.
  iv. Full Connection : This output is now connected to the final classification model,which acts as input of the fully connected ANN model.

